<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">British Columbia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">British Columbia is the westernmost province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, between the Rocky Mountains and the Pacific. Created as a British colony on the mainland in 1858 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fraser-river">Fraser River</a> gold rush, it was merged with the Colony of Vancouver Island in 1866. It joined Canada in 1871 on the promise of a transcontinental railway, completed in 1885.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/british-columbia.jpg" alt="British Columbia" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kooma (original) Sshu94 (current) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_British_Columbia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
